course: dictionary
lesson: 8980
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning its own number, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «A siren and flashing blue lights mean police are rushing to an emergency» uses siren as a warning sound, because the lights and the rushing police make that clear.
explain: Siren has a second meaning too: a creature from Greek myths. The Sirens were said to sing so beautifully that sailors steered their ships onto the rocks. If a sentence talks about singing that lures sailors, the myth meaning is the right one, not the alarm.
explain: Ask yourself: does this meaning fit the sentence? Put your meaning in place of the word and check. A warning sound fits «sirens wailing» well, but it would make no sense in a story about singing creatures on the rocks.
fact: A siren is a device that makes a loud wailing or rising-and-falling sound.
fact: Sirens warn people of danger: ambulances, fire engines and police cars use them, and drivers pull over to let them through.
fact: In Greek myths, the Sirens were creatures whose beautiful singing lured sailors onto rocks.
fact: A siren sounds higher as it comes towards you and lower as it goes away. Scientists call this the Doppler effect.
fact: When you hear a siren, look around, stay on the pavement and let the emergency vehicle pass.
exercise: «A siren and flashing blue lights mean police are rushing to an emergency.» What is a siren here? | A creature that sings to sailors | A kind of flashing light | A road with lots of bends | *A loud warning sound from a police car
exercise: In Greek myths, the Sirens sang so beautifully that sailors steered onto the rocks. What were the Sirens in the myths? | *Creatures whose singing lured sailors | Fire engines | Brave sailors who sang songs | Warning alarms at school
exercise: «A siren sounds higher as it comes towards you.» What does this sentence tell you about a siren? | It only works at night | *Its sound changes as it moves | It is always silent | It is made of stone
test: «Some sounds are made on purpose to warn you: sirens, car horns, smoke alarms and bike bells all say pay attention now.» Which of these is a siren? | A quiet whisper | A bird's song | *A loud warning sound
test: In a story, a siren is a dangerous, tempting singer. What does siren mean in this story? | *A creature who sings to lure sailors | Ambulance | Fire alarm | Warning light
exam: Which meaning of siren fits best in «The sailors heard a siren singing from the rocks»? | Police car | Flashing blue light | Warning sound from a fire engine | *A creature from Greek myths whose singing lured sailors
